  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - WEATHER RADAR NETWORK, through Government of Morocco</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USTDA is providing a $350,000 grant to the Moroccan National Meteorology Department to fund a feasibility study (FS) on the installation of an upgraded and expanded national weather radar network to increase coverage throughout the Kingdom of Morocco. The FS analyzes the benefits of improved radar coverage, including the ability to predict and respond to the occurrence of natural phenomena that could cause devastating loss of life and injury, severe damage to the environment, and destruction of the local economy. The FS recommends the most appropriate technical solution for upgrading and expanding the existing weather radar network in Morocco and also develops a procurement plan and bidding documents for the recommended technical solution.</narrative>
  </description>
